## IEEE 1800 reference

IEEE 1800-2017 and 1800-2023 §11.5.1 specify that an invalid bit-select address, including an out-of-bounds address, yields X for a four-state value. Both editions' §6.12.1 prohibit real-number index expressions of vector bit/part selects. Preserve these rules in both editions.

